EXPC-GVP — Licensing Status (Phase 00 Foundation)
==================================================

This file records the current licensing status of this repository. It is a
foundation-stage statement, not a final legal determination for every part
of the project.

1. Code and tooling
--------------------

Original code and tooling authored in this repository (e.g. anything that
will later appear under `tools/`, `schema/`, `tests/`) is licensed under the
MIT License, reproduced below. This choice covers **code only**.

2. Curated / aggregated data
-----------------------------

No licensing model has been selected yet for the curated/aggregated
vocabulary data that lives (or will eventually live) under `data/`. As of
Phase 00.2, `data/curated/` contains a small curator-authored fixture/test
dataset (see `SOURCES.md`, `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`) used only to validate
`schema/gvp.schema.json`; no external data has been imported, and no license
has been chosen for this or any future dataset content.

3. OPEN DECISIONS (not yet resolved)
-------------------------------------

The following must be explicitly decided and recorded in a future Source
Policy review before any data import takes place:

- OPEN: final license for curated/aggregated data produced by this project.
- OPEN: compatibility review of external source licenses/terms before any
  external source is imported (per-source, see `SOURCES.md`).
- OPEN: provenance requirements and how provenance is recorded per entry.
- OPEN: database rights and redistribution constraints that may apply in
  jurisdictions recognizing sui generis database rights, and how those
  constraints interact with redistribution of a compiled data package.

No claim is made in this repository about rights to any external data. No
external data has been imported.

